{"name":"Sweet Bianca","hex":"#eedadd","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bianca","blocks":[{"text":"Bianca is a feminine given name. It means \"white\" and is an Italian cognate of Blanche. It is known in the Anglosphere as a character in William Shakespeare's The Taming of the Shrew. It came to greater notice in the 1970s, due to public figures such as Bianca Jagger."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d2/Frederick_leighton-bianca_c1881_0876.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bianca"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Frederick_leighton-bianca_c1881_0876.jpg/250px-Frederick_leighton-bianca_c1881_0876.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d2/Frederick_leighton-bianca_c1881_0876.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Frederick_leighton-bianca_c1881_0876.jpg/250px-Frederick_leighton-bianca_c1881_0876.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrederick_leighton-bianca_c1881_0876.jpg"}],"sounds":{"sweet":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d7/En-us-sweet.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d7/En-us-sweet.ogg/En-us-sweet.ogg.mp3"}]}}}